# EA1-only kernel config, on top of board/ea/common/linux/common.fragment.
# Reachability is Wi-Fi (AR9485, mainline ath9k); the EA3 has no radio.

# --- kernel command line (EA1) ---
# pci=realloc,nocrs is REQUIRED: CEFDK leaves the ath9k/e1000 BARs unassigned and
# this is the combination proven to bring up wlan0. Do NOT copy to another board
# without checking its E820 (see the EA3 fragment, where `nocrs` breaks the NIC).
# pci=routeirq enables the CE5300 UART interrupt link (LUAR/GSI 38) for the IO-MCU
# on ttyS1 — see board/ea/common/linux/common.fragment.
#
# --- RAM reclaim (EA1) --------------------------------------------------------
# CEFDK withholds ~90% of DRAM. MEASURED on this EA1 (10.0.0.127): MemTotal only
# 180384 kB because e820 hands Linux just [0x00100000-0x0c7fffff] (200 MB) and
# marks [0x0c800000-0x7fffffff] (1.8 GB) "device reserved" — the Intel CE media
# carve-out. That range is REAL, IDLE DRAM (read-only over /dev/mem it still holds
# CEFDK's boot-time address-walk pattern up to ~0x7f000000). The e820 split, ACPI
# window and low-memory layout are byte-identical to the EA3-v2, whose reclaim is
# PROVEN on hardware, so the same line applies.
#
# memmap=exactmap is MANDATORY: the additive form is silently dropped (e820
# sanitisation resolves overlaps toward the HIGHER type, so "reserved" beats added
# "RAM"). Each entry is load-bearing — see ea3-v2.fragment for the full derivation
# (60K#0x11000 = ACPI tables; claiming them as RAM gives AE_NO_ACPI_TABLES + hang).
# 1536M@0x10000000 ends at 0x70000000, matching the EA3's proven margin. Do NOT
# widen past 0x70000000 without re-measuring: a memmap past real DRAM is
# unrecoverable remotely.
#
# GRADING: the e820/DRAM facts are measured on this EA1; the memmap line is the
# EA3-v2's PROVEN line on a verified-identical map, but has NOT yet been booted
# with it on an EA1 — confirm on hardware (a kexec is recoverable) and promote to
# "proven" once MemTotal reads back ~1.7 GB.
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=ttyS0,115200 earlyprintk=serial,ttyS0,115200 pci=realloc,nocrs,routeirq memmap=exactmap memmap=68K@0 memmap=60K#0x11000 memmap=512K@0x20000 memmap=255M@1M memmap=1536M@0x10000000"
